  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added the new names and kept the old ones as deprecated aliases. The unit tests pass (39/39) and `npm run arch` finds no new violations.\n\n**Why not a straight rename:** ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` from other repos. Renaming `totalCents` and `placedAt` would break them as soon as this deployed. The rule requires changes to be additive, with renames going through deprecation.\n\n**What changed**\n- `src/core/events.ts`: `OrderPlaced` now carries `createdAt` and `amountCents`. They have the same values as `placedAt` and `totalCents`. The old fields are marked `@deprecated`. `schemaVersion` stays 3 because the change is additive.\n- `test/app.test.ts`: the event assertions now cover both the new and old fields.\n\nI left the HTTP API alone. The `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` response bodies still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n\n**To finish the rename:** once both consumers have moved to the new names, remove `placedAt` and `totalCents` from the event. You'd probably also want to bump `schemaVersion` then.",
